# Project overview

Local Windows web app: scrape configured gallery sources or link local media, SQLite + files, React viewer (tags, ratings, duplicates, settings hide). Prefer **current code** over `README.md` when they disagree.

## Stack

| Layer | Stack |
|--------|--------|
| Frontend | React 18, TS, Vite 6, RR7, React Query 5; `frontend/src/index.css` |
| Backend | FastAPI, Uvicorn, SQLAlchemy 2, pydantic-settings |
| DB | SQLite `data/app.db` via `backend/init_db.py` (not Alembic-first) |
| Scraper | Obscura (preferred) or Playwright Chromium, BS4, httpx, **curl_cffi** |
| Launcher | `Run.bat` → `launcher.py` (venv, VERSION gate, install/update outside tools; scrape-only tools only when the Scrape page is on, build, tray) |

## Layout

`Run.bat`, `Update.bat`, `VERSION`, `versioning.py`, `launcher.py`, `adapters/example/` (sample package; other `adapters/*` gitignored), local `TODO.md` (gitignored; selection UI is the Project TODO canvas), `requirements.txt`, `backend/`, `frontend/`, `tests/`, `scripts/`, gitignored `data/` (incl. `data/adapters/`) + `media/`.

## Run / verify

- Normal: `Run.bat`. After changes: `Run.bat restart` or in-app Reload. Remote update: `Update.bat` (git pull, or ZIP merge if not a clone) updates files only — it does not launch; run `Run.bat` afterward to start/rebuild.
- Version gate: bump tracked `VERSION` when recipients should rebuild after update. Launch compares it to `data/installed_version` (stamped after a successful forced update; first value `0.1`). Mismatch stops a running app, forces pip + frontend rebuild, then starts; match does light ensures and opens the viewer if already healthy.
- Health: `http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/health` — on failure read `data/server.log`.
- UI change: `cd frontend && npm run build`.
- Order/tags changes: `scripts\run_order_tests.bat` (also via `.cursor/hooks.json` after edits to order/tag paths). See `testing.mdc`.
- Prefer minimal diffs; do not commit secrets, `.env`, `data/`, `media/`, `frontend/dist`, `.venv`.
- After behavior changes: update matching `.cursor/rules/*.mdc` and `README.md` (add/remove stale).
